      text: 'Traverse v0.16.0 (November 2, 2026) is a minor lockstep release with four breaking changes. 1) Exact-ref model registration takes the execution policy (Spec 138 0.16.0, Decision 120): pass policy_ref, placements and require_fuel_metering when you register, register every policy_ref you call, expect slower registration and faster first calls, and stop passing placements on calls. 2) Every host gives guests RFC 8785 (JCS) canonical JSON input (Decision 118); input JCS cannot represent fails with input_not_canonicalizable, and Rust ExecutorError gains InputNotCanonicalizable. 3) Hosts enforce the contract inputs.schema before the artifact runs (#1658): unknown fields under additionalProperties: false and strings over maxLength fail with invalid_input / RequestInvalid. 4) Registry rights fail closed (Spec 045 1.1.0, #1728): ranges skip revoked versions, an exact pin to a revoked version fails closed with the revocation record, and conditional model rights need an explicit host opt-in. Building from source needs Rust 1.95. Use the onnx-runner-v0.16.0 runner. traverse-mcp Mode A now ships prebuilt binaries, so no Rust toolchain is needed. v0.16.0 also carries the wasmtime 48.0.7 security fix. crates.io, npm, Maven Central, nuget.org and SwiftPM are all at 0.16.0 (the crates landed on the afternoon of November 2). Discover → execute → trace is unchanged on one shared runtime.wasm.',
